R1-DASH — the e2e delta for the V3 Dashboard widening (Wave R).

WHAT IT CHANGES (two files, four hunks, no behaviour):

  e2e/parity.spec.ts   3 rows — incubator/{admin,program_manager,program_associate}/alldecks
                       title "All decks" -> "Dashboard", and the v15 seven-column
                       header set replaced by the V3 eight-column one. After this
                       they are byte-identical to the incubator/superuser row,
                       which is the point: the four staff roles share one screen.

  e2e/programs.spec.ts 1 assertion — that walk signs in as the incubator ADMIN
                       and reads the h1, which is now "Dashboard — Climate
                       Cohort". NOT a parity row; it is here because it is the
                       same one-line cause and splitting it makes it possible to
                       apply half the change.

WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT A COMMIT
  §4 of docs/plan_roles_incubator.md: EXPECTED is one flat record and every Wave
  R session would land a hunk in it, so the integration session owns the file.
  e2e/programs.spec.ts is R3-SETUP's by the same table.

HOW TO PLACE IT
  git apply --check docs/parity-requests/R1-parity.patch && \
  git apply docs/parity-requests/R1-parity.patch

  Verified with `git apply --check` against the R1-DASH tree at generation time.
  Order-independent with the other Wave R patches: no other session's row delta
  touches these three keys or that assertion.

IF THE CLIENT ANSWERS §6 Q-A AGAINST THE DEVIATION
  Revert this patch together with the `isV3Dash` predicate, the `alldecks`
  labelOverrides/iconOverrides and the five parity-nav EXPECTED_GAPS rows. They
  are one change; reverting any one of them alone leaves a sidebar and an H1
  disagreeing.

